.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt ARCANA-ENROL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arcana-enrol
.Nd join this host to a arcana console
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl a Ar address ...
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Ar console-url token
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
gets this host a certificate from the arcana console's certificate
authority, so that
.Xr arcana-agent 8
can serve the console over mutual TLS.
It makes an EC P-256 key and a certificate request, sends the request to
.Ar console-url
with the one-time
.Ar token
the console issued for this host, and writes what comes back:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "host.key" -compact -offset indent
.It Pa host.key
the private key, mode 0600;
.It Pa host.pem
the certificate, for the name the token was made for;
.It Pa ca.pem
the console's CA, which signs the console's own client certificate.
.El
.Pp
The files go to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana .
The console adds this host to its server list at the same time, as
.Pa tcp://host:port .
Then
.Nm
prints the
.Xr rc.conf 5
lines that run
.Xr arcana-agent 8
with the files, or sets them itself with
.Fl s .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl a Ar address
An address
.Xr arcana-agent 8
is to listen on, in the printed or applied flags; may be given more
than once.
The default is every address, over IPv4 and IPv6 both:
.Li 0.0.0.0
and
.Li \&:: .
.It Fl d Ar directory
Write the files there instead of
.Pa /usr/local/etc/arcana .
.It Fl n Ar name
The name in the certificate request.
The console ignores it and names the certificate after the token's host;
the default is this host's name.
.It Fl p Ar port
The port in the flags.
The default is 4310, the port the console will connect to unless the
token was made with another.
.It Fl s
Enable and start
.Xr arcana-agent 8
with
.Xr sysrc 8
and
.Xr service 8 :
it sets
.Va arcana_agent_enable
and the network listeners in
.Va arcana_agent_listen ,
and, with
.Fl d ,
where the files are in
.Va arcana_agent_ca ,
.Va arcana_agent_cert
and
.Va arcana_agent_key .
Without it the command to do so is printed.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
In the console, add a server with
.Dq Enrol a host ,
giving it a name and the host name or address the console reaches it by.
The console shows a command like
.Bd -literal -offset indent
arcana-enrol -s https://console.example 3f1c...
.Ed
.Pp
Run it on the host as root;
.Fl s
has
.Xr arcana-agent 8
enabled and running right away.
Options go before the URL, as
.Xr getopt 3
stops at the first argument.
The token works once and for an hour.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr arcana-agent 8 ,
.Xr arcana-console 8 ,
.Xr arcanactl 8
.Sh SECURITY
The console's own HTTPS certificate is checked by
.Xr fetch 3
against the system's trusted CAs.
Over plain HTTP, or with
.Ev SSL_NO_VERIFY_PEER
set, whoever can read the connection can take the token and have the
certificate issued to a key of their own.
.Pp
Once the console has answered,
.Nm
runs in capability mode
.Pq Xr capsicum 4 :
the answer is parsed and the files are written through the directory
opened beforehand, and nothing else of the system is reachable.
.Xr sysrc 8
and
.Xr service 8
are run by a child forked before that, told to go once the files are
in place.
